{
 "title": "Rebuild the Oldhand website for the 2.0 pack",
 "mode": "implement",
 "created": "2026-10-10T20:06:13+00:00",
 "criteria": [
  {
   "id": "AC1",
   "text": "The page renders the conductor skill's own text (skills/oldhand/SKILL.md imported at build time, not a copy) in a scrollable block with \"Copy raw\" and \"View on GitHub\" controls, and the hard stops section shown above it is sliced from that same import",
   "proof": "e2e",
   "status": "live",
   "added": "2026-10-10T20:06:13+00:00"
  },
  {
   "id": "AC2",
   "text": "An install switcher offers one tab per install route that was tested on this machine (Any agent via npx skills, Claude Code plugin, Codex plugin, git clone), each with the exact commands, a copy control that copies that exact text, the line to type afterwards per host, and the tool version and date it was tested; no untested command is shown",
   "proof": "e2e",
   "status": "live",
   "added": "2026-10-10T20:06:13+00:00"
  },
  {
   "id": "AC3",
   "text": "The page contains no invented artifact: no fake ids, stamps, fake screenshots, decorative checkmarks or status badges, and every factual claim links to its source file in the repository",
   "proof": "review",
   "status": "live",
   "added": "2026-10-10T20:06:13+00:00"
  },
  {
   "id": "AC4",
   "text": "The page is readable in light and dark (prefers-color-scheme) at 1440 and 375 wide with no horizontal page scroll, no text under 13px, and text and the primary control meet WCAG AA contrast",
   "proof": "e2e",
   "status": "live",
   "added": "2026-10-10T20:06:13+00:00"
  },
  {
   "id": "AC5",
   "text": "Google Analytics is not loaded on first visit; the only control is a footer toggle; choosing it loads GA and the choice persists across reload; there is no overlay or banner",
   "proof": "e2e",
   "status": "live",
   "added": "2026-10-10T20:06:13+00:00"
  },
  {
   "id": "AC6",
   "text": "An \"Example run\" section shows the real examples/csv-import-dupes run: its verdict line, criteria table and \"Not verified\" section sliced from the committed report.md, with a link to the files",
   "proof": "e2e",
   "status": "live",
   "added": "2026-10-10T20:06:13+00:00"
  },
  {
   "id": "AC7",
   "text": "The page lists the 11 stages in chain order, one line each, every line linking to that stage's SKILL.md on GitHub, and a model routing table by role (lead, worker, scout) per host with the substitution note, dated",
   "proof": "e2e",
   "status": "live",
   "added": "2026-10-10T20:06:13+00:00"
  },
  {
   "id": "R1",
   "text": "`npm run build` and `npm run test:sites` pass; dist/client/index.html, dist/server/index.js and dist/.openai/hosting.json still exist",
   "proof": "integration",
   "status": "live",
   "added": "2026-10-10T20:06:13+00:00"
  },
  {
   "id": "R2",
   "text": "The GitHub Pages workflow still works unchanged: it builds site/, previews on 127.0.0.1:4173, and screenshots `?social-preview=1` at 1200x627 into dist/client/og-image.png, so the social-preview hook in index.html must survive",
   "proof": "review",
   "status": "live",
   "added": "2026-10-10T20:06:13+00:00"
  },
  {
   "id": "R3",
   "text": "The existing opt-in analytics code path keeps consent default denied and never loads gtag before a stored \"granted\" choice",
   "proof": "unit",
   "status": "live",
   "added": "2026-10-10T20:06:13+00:00"
  }
